cerberus (0.15.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  Packaging correctness, one client warning, and a dependency refresh. The API
  and the signer carry no change beyond their dependencies: certificate
  issuance, authorization, the enclave protocol and the configuration surface
  are all untouched, so a server-side upgrade needs nothing but the new
  packages. UPGRADE NOTE: /etc/profile.d/cssh.sh is no longer a conffile.

  * UPGRADE NOTE: /etc/profile.d/cssh.sh is now a symlink to
    /usr/lib/cerberus/cssh.sh, and no longer a dpkg conffile. cssh.sh is
    program code; the RPM and Arch packages have always replaced it on upgrade,
    but as a conffile it was frozen once an admin edited it, so the hosts most
    likely to need a fix were exactly the ones that stopped receiving it. If
    you had modified the file, this upgrade preserves your copy as
    /etc/profile.d/cssh.sh.dpkg-bak -- kept for reference, no longer in effect
    -- and the live path becomes the current script. cerberus-env.sh is
    untouched and remains this package's one conffile: it is site config, and
    your edits there survive upgrades.
  * Verified rather than assumed, by building both releases and upgrading
    across them with the real packages. With both files edited by hand,
    cssh.sh comes out byte-identical to the shipped 0.15.0 script while the
    cerberus-env.sh edit is kept; with neither edited, both take the new
    shipped content. The RPM behaves identically (plain file vs
    %config(noreplace)). Note that dpkg prompts about an edited
    cerberus-env.sh when its shipped default also changed, and an unattended
    apt run keeps your copy; dnf writes .rpmnew without prompting.
  * cssh warns on stderr before connecting when the certificate carries
    permit-session-renewal@cerberus but cerberus-session is not on PATH. That
    combination silently drops the renewal bridge, and the failure otherwise
    surfaces only later and elsewhere, as "this session has no renewal bridge"
    from logsh on the server. The session still opens; only renewal is
    unavailable. The certificate's extension list is parsed once and shared
    with the login-as check, so a connect still makes one ssh-keygen call.
  * build-rpm.sh staged its working-tree packaging/ overlay with
    "cp -a packaging" onto a directory git archive had already created, so the
    overlaid files landed at packaging/packaging/ where the spec never looks,
    and every source tarball carried a duplicate copy of the packaging tree.
    It now merge-copies the contents, as the Debian and Arch builders already
    did. Build-time only: a build from a clean checkout was never affected,
    since the tracked copies come out of git archive either way.
  * rsync is documented as a prerequisite for build-deb.sh and build-arch.sh.
    Both fall back to it when the tree is not a usable git work tree -- an
    exported tarball, or a worktree whose .git the build cannot follow -- and
    only build-rpm.sh said so, which left a container build dying at
    "rsync: command not found" after the documented deps were installed.
  * ssh-cert-api is tidy again after the root module's x/crypto bump. The
    submodules replace the root, so MVS selected a version their own go.sum
    did not carry and every ssh-cert-api CI leg failed with "updates to go.mod
    needed"; x/crypto and x/sys now move in all three modules together.
  * docs: the stale "noarch" descriptions of cerberus-client are corrected
    across the three packagings and the runbook, and docs/cssh.md states the
    upgrade contract for cssh.sh and cerberus-env.sh in each format's own
    terms rather than only the RPM's.
  * Dependencies: golang.org/x/crypto 0.57.0 -> 0.58.0 and golang.org/x/sys
    0.48.0 -> 0.49.0 in all three modules. AWS SDK v2 refresh in both service
    modules: core 1.47.1 -> 1.47.3, kms 1.61.2 -> 1.61.4 (the attested Decrypt
    the host performs on the enclave's behalf), config 1.33.7 -> 1.33.9,
    credentials 1.20.7 -> 1.20.9, sts 1.51.2 -> 1.51.4, imds 1.20.1 -> 1.20.3,
    smithy-go 1.28.1 -> 1.28.5, plus the signin, sso, ssooidc, v4a,
    presigned-url, accept-encoding, configsources and endpoints set.
    ssh-cert-api additionally moves prometheus/client_golang 1.24.1 -> 1.25.0
    and prometheus/common 0.71.0 -> 0.72.0.
  * CI and "make test-cssh" gain tests/cssh_renewal_bridge_test.sh, run under
    bash and zsh beside the existing sidecar, login-as and extend suites.
  * govulncheck reports no vulnerabilities reachable from any module.

